SWEET WLAN live scan in keep mode (patch 0292, WIFI-COVERAGE D3/D4: Settings > Wi-Fi lists the networks around; branch wlan/rejoin, builds on 0268/0281/0282/0288). Before, Set 10 SCAN_REQ replayed the BOOT-TIME scan (stale). Now, with the kept link, Set 10 asks the keep thread for a real scan and returns at once (sweet_wlan_keep_scan_request: one flag, no engine access); the keep thread (swl25_sc_step, once per pass under the en0 lock, BEFORE the re-join step) sends ONE firmware command, WLC_SET_VAR "escan" (the passive START of the boot scan L23 in its all-channel form: channel_num 0 = the firmware's own channel list, 80 B, scan_type passive, default home time, own sync id; built by the one builder swg_e_escan_arg that the boot scan uses too, with chans 0; the BOOT scan keeps its 7 channels 1 6 11 36 40 44 48 at lv >= 24, sync 0x1234), and collects the ESCAN_RESULT events (WLC_E 69, status 8 = PARTIAL one bss record, 0 = SUCCESS) from ring 2 through swg_ke_event -> swg_ke_escan -> sweet_wlan_a80211_scan_event into a scratch table (the radio's own parser swr_event: dedupe by BSSID keeping the stronger RSSI, 64 records). When SUCCESS is seen, or after 12 s (SWL25_SC_BUDGET_MS; a passive scan of ~38 channels with home-channel returns may need ~6 s [guess]) with a GAP, or when the AP link is lost, the thread (outside the lock) calls sweet_wlan_a80211_scan_done: the list is swapped in and SCAN_DONE (kev 10) is posted; wifid's Get 11 loop then iterates the list and ends with EIO (unverified end code, GAP in the sta handler). Rules: one scan at a time; refused with a GAP while the kept link is DOWN (re-join owns the engine, errno 50) or while one is pending (errno 16); a link loss ENDS a running scan first (no abort command is sent), the re-join machine never runs while a scan runs; a soft stop inside the escan ioctl turns the scan off for the boot (GAP) and Set 10 then falls back to the stale boot-time list, loudly; the RSSI refresh pauses during a scan. Logs: one line per scan start and done with counts only, never an SSID or BSSID. NEW firmware command: WLC_SET_VAR escan (86 B = "escan\0" + 80 B), whitelist row 19 {"escan", SET_VAR, 86, CHK_ESCAN} with the payload checked byte for byte (swl25w_chk_escan, version 2 or 3). The headers (sweet_wlan_g2.h, g2e.h, l25_hs.h, l25_wl.h) are regenerated in patches 0174 and 0206 and sweet_wlan_radio.h / sweet_wlan_a80211.c in 0201 from shim/. Review 0292 fixes: each keep scan has its own sync_id (0x1235..0x1333, the boot scan keeps 0x1234) and the judge row 19 takes the expected id of the scan being sent (exactly it, inside that range); events of another sync id are a GAP on the first and every 64th and are counted in the scan-end line; a firmware end status other than SUCCESS/PARTIAL (abort 4, new scan 9, new assoc 10 ...) ends the scan at once with a GAP naming it; a link loss that ends a running scan holds the first re-join attempt until the firmware reports the scan's end status or 2 s pass (GAP if not), still with no abort command; the request/abort pair at thread end is seq_cst. Not run on hardware; the new write path is unreviewed.
